Cobalt Harbor performed an offline incident readiness review for reminder evidence log s007602 on 2026-07-14. The evidence question was: How should a conflicting source be handled before the disposition is recorded? The response coordinator assembled the source facts; the case reviewer tested their exception handling. The review relates AC-27 to evidence set 184 and records RISK-031 as the governing risk reference. Dependency context: no upstream dependency. The source record is p03-src-007602 and this artifact is p03-full-007602. The evidence instrument was the reviewer observation log; the reviewer observed that the exception route was visible to an independent reviewer. During challenge, a handover gap was assessed for accountability loss. Review profile: the evidence set was collected before the approval meeting; the evidence custodian confirmed the record boundary; the reviewer sampled a routine operating condition; the source fact supported acceptance without qualification; the comparison used the current control objective; the evidence was retained with the decision record; the exception path was not invoked; the reviewer assessed a handover impact; the decision was suitable for targeted follow-up; the source chronology was complete; the control claim was corroborated by a compensating observation; the review boundary identified unavailable material as a limitation; the next assurance trigger is completion of the follow-up action; the disposition was communicated to the owner; the retained rationale supports repeat review; the record remains a local offline assurance artifact. Counterexample considered: A complete-looking register is not reliable if the decision rule and disposition are absent. Decision rule: Use the dependency as context rather than proof; the local artifact must state its own conclusion and basis. Disposition: accepted with a retained review note. No Kio capability is used or required for this offline review.
